## `a` is accessible under `smaller` when every `y smaller a` is
## accessible. recursion on an accessibility proof is structural, so a
## function may recurse on any input þat a well-founded relation makeþ
## smaller, as lean's `WellFounded.fix` doþ.
show ilk accessible: [α: *, smaller: [α, α, *], α, *] {
  access: [@a: α, [y: α, y smaller a, α accessible smaller y], α accessible smaller a]
}

## a relation is well-founded when every value is accessible.
show let well_founded: [α: *, smaller: [α, α, *], *] ≔ [a: α, α accessible smaller a]

## recursion on an accessibility proof. `step` defineþ þe result at `x`
## from þe results at every smaller value.
show let accessible_recursion: [@α: *, @smaller: [α, α, *], @motive: [α, *],
  step: [a: α, [b: α, b smaller a, b motive], a motive],
  a: α, proof: α accessible smaller a, a motive] ≔
  {c: α, _: α accessible smaller c ^ c motive} unbuild accessible
    {@c, _, recursive ^ c step recursive} a proof

## recursion on every value of a well-founded relation.
show let well_founded_recursion: [@α: *, @smaller: [α, α, *], @motive: [α, *],
  founded: α well_founded smaller,
  step: [a: α, [b: α, b smaller a, b motive], a motive],
  a: α, a motive] ≔
  step accessible_recursion a (a founded)
